# Files that hang UBS Meta-Runner v5.3.11 — the source-of-truth skip list.
#
# bd-yxsqo: ubs hangs (>10 min, superlinear) on large Rust files. Measured
# 2026-08-17: connection.rs (270k lines) and pager.rs (55k lines) both time out at
# >90s; codegen.rs (55k) is the same class. The pathology triggers somewhere below
# 55k lines, on a single explicit file, and even with --skip-type-narrowing.
#
# IMPORTANT: ubs v5.3.11 does NOT actually honor this file as ignore globs —
# verified that explicit-file scans AND directory walks still hang with it present.
# It is instead the machine-readable filter list for the AGENTS.md-documented
# invocation, which strips these paths BEFORE ubs sees them:
#
#     ubs $(git diff --name-only --cached | grep -vxFf .ubsignore)
#
# Entries are exact repo-relative paths (as `git diff --name-only` prints them).
# Coverage note: these files still get clippy + `cargo check` + the test suites;
# only the ubs pass is skipped. Shrinking the connection.rs god-object (bd-oxw4d)
# restores ubs coverage. If a NEW ubs scan hangs, the file is too big — add it here.
crates/fsqlite-core/src/connection.rs
crates/fsqlite-pager/src/pager.rs
crates/fsqlite-vdbe/src/codegen.rs
